  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "6ec99b20-bdf1-49d3-abc6-f5ba07ae39bf",
      "phaseId": "1df9c36c-5c29-4288-9fe1-7a6e9c72179b",
      "number": 279,
      "shortId": "GWVX6",
      "priority": 2,
      "shortName": "choice-2-refactor-select-to-co",
      "title": "choice-2: Refactor `Select` to compose `Choice` children (the hard one — overlay + scroll)",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Make `Select` (`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/select.rs`) **compose its options as `Choice` children** instead of hand-drawing them.\n\n## DONE 2026-07-14 — user tested and approved (\"works perfect\"). Branch `feat/viewnode-choice-select`.\n\n## How the hard part was solved\n**taffy measures, `Select` places.** The options are `Choice` children laid out in the trigger's flow — where the engine measures them (each hugs its content; `flex_shrink: 0` is already the library default, so they keep their natural heights). `Select` then *places* them, baking the offset from that flow into their bounds — the `ScrollRegion` trick, now shared: `shift_subtree` was promoted from `scroll_region.rs` to `component.rs` (`pub(crate)`).\n\nInvariant: **bounds === what is drawn === what is clickable.** Picks go through `choice_at()` (real bounds, never row arithmetic). Rows outside the visible window — and every row while closed except the chosen one — are **collapsed to zero size**, so no stale rect can swallow a click. Placement is re-derived in `on_layout`, idempotent (absolute targets; never compounds).\n\n- Row heights are **measured, not arithmetic** (`natural_h`, captured post-layout) → a two-line option stacks correctly. The flip/cap fit test reserves the *tallest* row (conservative → never clipped).\n- The control's horizontal insets ride on the rows as **margins** (not padding on the Select): that widens the control around them *and* keeps option content clear of the chevron + scrollbar lane. Padding could not do both.\n- Trigger **width hugs the widest option** (engine-measured, icons included — the char-count estimate is gone); **height** hugs the tallest option, so it can stand any of them in it.\n\n## The trigger shows the chosen option ITSELF (icon and all), open or closed\nClosed, the option *is* the trigger's content — `place_options` stands that child in the trigger slot. Open, it has moved into the list (a component is laid out in exactly one place), so the trigger draws a second **image** of its content via the new `PaintCx::with_translate`. Only content is echoed, never the row's chrome (the trigger's box is its chrome; a pill inside it would be a box in a box) — hence `sync_option_states` ties \"selected\" to `open`.\n\n## 3 generic library additions (all forced by the above, all documented in `docs/widgets.md` + rustdoc)\n- **`PaintCx::with_translate(dx, dy, |cx| …)`** — paint a subtree somewhere else. One choke point (`PaintCx::placed`) covers every draw helper + the cull test, so **no renderer change**. Rule written into the docs: what it draws is **NOT interactive** (no bounds ⇒ not hit-tested/focusable/hoverable); never use it to *move* a widget — that is `shift_subtree` + `on_layout`, which keeps bounds honest.\n- **`Component::text_summary()`** — accessible name of composed content (default: first child that has one; `Label` supplies it). Powers `selected_label()`: a control reading the *text* of content whose type it cannot see.\n- **`Style::align_self` + `LayoutExt::align_self`** (CSS `align-self`). Without it an `Auto`-width control silently goes full-width in a column parent (default `align: Stretch`) — the width hug would have been a regression.\n\n## User test round → 3 fixes (all in)\n1. **Hover bled through the open panel** (a Button underneath lit up): the panel now **consumes `PointerMoved`** over itself. Root cause: the host offers events to the overlay first and only falls through on `Handled::No`; `Select` never consumed moves. Pre-existing, exposed by the refactor.\n2. **Trigger lost the icon while open** → fixed with `with_translate` (above).\n3. Docs: added the **declarative `ViewNode` example** (both audiences, per AGENTS).\n\n## API\n`Select::new([..])` unchanged — sugar building `Choice::labeled(text, text)` children (every call site compiles). New: `Select::empty()` + `.option(Choice)` — typed to `Choice` on purpose (it keeps the row's `state()` signal to flip selection in place; `Box<dyn Component>` would erase it). **`Parent` is deliberately NOT implemented** — so choice-4's realize arm must build `Choice` typed (a `realize_choice`), not via generic `realize`. `selected_label()` now returns `String` (was `&str`). Preserved: `overlay_active()`, flip/cap, scroll + scrollbar + wheel, `MenuUp`/`MenuDown`/`Activate`/`Dismiss`, the `select-change` payload, `.selected(i)`, `.state()`, `.index()`. `focus_barrier` on. The cursor highlight stays the container's chrome (keeps the `hilite` token); selection is the `Choice`'s own state (accent pill + tinted content).\n\n## Tests (+3 → heca-grid-ui 137)\nsugar builds `Choice` children · composed icon+label option: trigger shows icon AND label **while open**, chosen row tints its content accent · click resolves from the child's **real bounds** (the two old tests that hardcoded `ROW_H = 30` arithmetic now read bounds) · off-window + closed rows collapsed/unclickable · flips above the trigger at the viewport edge.\n\n## Gates\nclippy `--workspace --all-targets --all-features` 0 warnings (only the pre-existing transitive `block v0.1.6` note) · heca-grid-ui **137** + 71 + 1 · heca 335 · showcase green (new composed LEVEL `Select` with icon+label options). No `cargo fmt`.\n\n## Files\n`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/select.rs` (rewrite), `component.rs` (`with_translate`, `text_summary`, `shift_subtree`), `style.rs` + `builders.rs` (`align_self`), `label.rs` (`text_summary`), `choice.rs` (`BASE_PAD` → `pub(crate)`), `scroll_region.rs` (shared `shift_subtree`), `tests/phase_a.rs`, `heca-renderer/examples/showcase.rs`, `docs/widgets.md`.\n\n## NEXT\n**choice-3** (`7ef645d5`) — `Tabs` onto `Choice` children. Its sliding underline should now animate between the selected child's **real bounds** (a simplification), and `Tabs` gets the same treatment: sugar → `Choice::labeled` children, `focus_barrier`, no monospace-metric arithmetic.",
