    {
      "id": "bfc43fce-a202-414c-a3f6-0d87a50547e8",
      "phaseId": "1df9c36c-5c29-4288-9fe1-7a6e9c72179b",
      "number": 281,
      "shortId": "RXA77",
      "priority": 4,
      "shortName": "choice-4-realize-arms-choice-s",
      "title": "choice-4: realize arms — `Choice`, `Select`, `Tabs` (+ value→intent args)",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Add the `realize` arms so the option-shaped widgets are authorable declaratively, and make the **chosen value** flow back to the author.\n\n## STATUS: code complete on `feat/viewnode-choice-select` (uncommitted). No UI surface to test by hand — `realize` is the host bridge, covered by unit tests. Awaiting the user's go-ahead to commit.\n\n## Done (`heca/src/chrome/{view.rs, realize.rs}`)\n1. **`WidgetKind::Choice`** — new variant. Props: `value` (`Text`/`Int` — what the option *means*), `text` as the **childless sugar** (→ one `Label` child). Precedence: **children win** (identical rule to `Button`). With no `value`, the text stands in for it, so `Choice { text: \"HIGH\" }` matches the native `Choice::labeled`.\n2. **`realize` arms** — `Choice`, `Select`, `Tabs`:\n   - `realize_choice(node) -> Choice` — **typed**, not `Box<dyn Component>`, because `Select::option` / `Tabs::tab` are typed (they keep the option's state signals to drive selection in place; a boxed component would have erased them). This is why choice-2/3 deliberately did **not** implement `Parent` on those widgets.\n   - `realize_options()` — the `Choice` children in order; a child of any other kind is **ignored** with a debug log (realize stays total for untrusted input).\n   - `Select`/`Tabs` read `selected` (Int, via a new `usize_prop` that rejects negatives) and wire `change`.\n   - A **standalone** `Choice` gets its `press` intent wired (`on_activate` + hint target). Inside a `Select`/`Tabs` the container owns the click, so a `press` there is ignored rather than half-wired.\n3. **Value → intent args** (`option_change`) — the point of the whole model. The widgets emit an index (`SignalData::Usize`); `realize` captures the options' `value` props at realize time and maps the index back through them, dispatching the bound `Intent` with **`args[\"value\"]`** set → a plugin receives `{\"value\": \"high\"}`, never an opaque `1` that breaks the moment the options are reordered. No `value` on the option → falls back to `args[\"index\"]`.\n4. No closures cross the boundary; the `press`/`change` vocabulary is unchanged (AGENTS ⛔ SETTLED).\n\n## Tests (+5 → heca 340)\n`select_node_realizes_its_choice_children_as_options` (children become options; each composes its own icon+label; named by `text_summary`) · **`the_change_intent_carries_the_chosen_options_value_not_its_index`** (realize → layout → open the dropdown → click the second row *at its real bounds* → the emitted `InteractionIntent::View` carries `args[\"value\"] = \"high\"`) · `tabs_node_realizes_choice_children_and_reports_the_chosen_value` (same mapping via `ItemNext`) · `childless_choice_node_desugars_its_text_to_a_label_child` · `a_non_choice_child_of_a_select_is_ignored`. Also fixed `deferred_kind_is_empty_not_panic`, which used `Tabs` as its \"deferred kind\" — now realized, so it tests `Grid`.\n\n## Docs\n`view.rs` rustdoc: props/events table gains `Choice`/`Select`/`Tabs`, plus an \"Options are children\" section (the value→intent rule, the two totality rules). `docs/widgets.md`: the model table + a new **\"Options are children (`Select` / `Tabs` / `Choice`)\"** section; the `Choice` entry gains its declarative examples; the \"not realized yet\" list is down to `Grid` / `ItemGroup` / `DockFrame` / `MarkerGroup` / `Toast`, with `ScrollBar` documented as **host-only** by design.\n**AGENTS.md ⭐ block updated**: the \"Genuinely OPEN\" list no longer claims `Select`/`Tabs`/`Button` realize coverage is open; a **SETTLED since** paragraph now records composition, options-as-children + value→intent, content-color inheritance, and host-only `ScrollBar`.\n\n## Gates (2026-07-14)\nclippy `--workspace --all-targets --all-features` 0 warnings · heca **340** · heca-grid-ui 138 + 71 + 1 · showcase builds. No `cargo fmt`.\n\n## NEXT\n**choice-5** (`fdbcabf3`) — realize arms for `ItemGroup` + `MarkerGroup` (no model change needed; `ItemGroup` introduces the `toggle` event name).",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [
