    },
    {
      "id": "fdbcabf3-eaa5-4983-9d36-75f393cb0b44",
      "phaseId": "1df9c36c-5c29-4288-9fe1-7a6e9c72179b",
      "number": 282,
      "shortId": "YQE75",
      "priority": 5,
      "shortName": "choice-5-realize-arms-itemgrou",
      "title": "choice-5: realize arms — `ItemGroup` + `MarkerGroup` (no model change needed)",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "The two easy kinds: both already expressible with the model as it stands (text + bools + children + one event). Pure `realize` work, no widget refactor, no new `PropValue`.\n\n## DONE 2026-07-14 — heca 343, clippy clean. Host-bridge work with no UI surface; verified by tests.\n\n## Shipped (`heca/src/chrome/{view.rs, realize.rs}`)\n- **`ItemGroup` arm** — props `text` (header) + `expanded` (Bool, default `true`); children = the rows, appended **after** the widget's own header (`children[0]`). The group applies its expanded state in `remeasure`, so builder order doesn't matter and a collapsed group folds its rows out of layout on the first pass.\n- **`MarkerGroup` arm** — props `active` / `nav_selected` (Bool); children = the rows. **No events**: it is an indicator, and the rows inside carry their own intents (asserted in a test — it registers zero hint targets).\n- **`toggle`** — the third canonical event name, alongside `press`/`change`. `toggle_change()` dispatches the bound intent with **`args[\"expanded\"]`** set to the state the group moved to, so an author binds one action and learns which way it went instead of tracking the state on their side. This mirrors the value→intent rule from choice-4: an event carries what the author needs to act on, never a bare ping.\n\n## Tests (+3 → heca 343)\n`item_group_node_realizes_its_header_and_rows` (header + 2 rows; `expanded: false` folds the rows via `display: none` after a layout pass) · `the_toggle_intent_carries_the_new_expanded_state` (realize → layout → click the header → the emitted `InteractionIntent::View` carries `args[\"expanded\"] = false`) · `marker_group_node_realizes_its_rows_and_flags`.\n\n## Note worth keeping\n`Component::text_summary()`'s default is **first descendant text wins** — on an `ItemGroup` that is the header's *chevron glyph*, not the label. Correct behaviour (the chevron is a real `Label`), but it means the default accessible name is only meaningful for content-only subtrees (a `Choice`, a `Button`). Do not lean on it for widgets whose chrome includes text.\n\n## Docs\n`view.rs`: the `Events` rustdoc now lists the whole vocabulary (`press` / `change` / `toggle`) with what each intent carries; props table gains `ItemGroup`/`MarkerGroup`. `docs/widgets.md`: model table + an event-vocabulary paragraph; both entries gain **Native + Declarative** examples; the \"not realized yet\" list is down to `Grid` / `DockFrame` / `Toast` (+ host-only `ScrollBar`).\n\n## Gates\nclippy `--workspace --all-targets --all-features` 0 warnings · heca **343** · heca-grid-ui 138 + 71 + 1 · showcase builds. No `cargo fmt`.\n\n## NEXT\n**choice-6** (`2178830d`) — `PropValue::List` + the `Grid` realize arm (tracks as CSS-like strings, areas, per-child placement). The only kind left that genuinely needs a new model primitive.",
      "notes": "",
